{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":754,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.99,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 13 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". Count sequences with no run of 3 same bits. Classic Fibonacci-like. For length n, number of binary strings with no 3 consecutive equal bits. We can use recurrence: Let a_n be number of strings length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit? Actually easier: Use DP with states: last two bits? We need to avoid 3 same. So track last two bits. State: last two bits pattern. For n=1, we have 2 strings. For n=2, 4 strings. For n>=3, recurrence: For each string of length n-1, we can append bit if it doesn't create 3 same. Equivalent to DP with last two bits. Let's compute manually.\n\nLet dp[n][last_bit][run_length] where run_length 1 or 2. But simpler: Let A_n be number of strings length n ending with a run of length 1 (i.e., last two bits differ). Let B_n be number ending with run length 2 (i.e., last two bits same but previous different). For n=1: run length 1 only: A_1=2 (0 or1). B_1=0.\n\nTransition: To get A_{n+1}: we need last two bits differ. So we can append bit different from last bit. If previous run length 1 or 2, appending opposite bit resets run length to1. So A_{n+1} = A_n + B_n.\n\nTo get B_{n+1}: we need last two bits same, so we append same bit as last. But only allowed if previous run length was 1 (since if previous run length 2, appending same would make run length3 forbidden). So B_{n+1} = A_n.\n\nThus recurrence: A_{n+1}=A_n+B_n; B_{n+1}=A_n.\n\nWe can compute up to n=13.\n\nInitialize n=1: A1=2, B1=0.\n\nn=2: A2=A1+B1=2+0=2; B2=A1=2. Check total 4.\n\nn=3: A3=A2+B2=2+2=4; B3=A2=2. Total 6.\n\nn=4: A4= A3+B3=4+2=6; B4=A3=4. Total 10.\n\nn=5: A5=6+4=10; B5=6. Total 16.\n\nn=6: A6=10+6=16; B6=10. Total 26.\n\nn=7: A7=16+10=26; B7=16. Total 42.\n\nn=8: A8=26+16=42; B8=26. Total 68.\n\nn=9: A9=42+26=68; B9=42. Total 110.\n\nn=10: A10=68+42=110; B10=68. Total 178.\n\nn=11: A11=110+68=178; B11=110. Total 288.\n\nn=12: A12=178+110=288; B12=178. Total 466.\n\nn=13: A13=288+178=466; B13=288. Total 754.\n\nThus answer 754."}}],"created":1790956490,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4111,"total_tokens":4879,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-t114NFHX1Od9IerkKSzIOJDdzFnaksnh","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4111,"prompt_ms":488.163,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.11874556069082949,"prompt_per_second":8421.367453084318,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2356.561,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.0724393741851372,"predicted_per_second":325.47428222736437}}